Cambyses budget-only host selftests
==================================

Run from any directory:
  python3 -I /home/ssx/android-kernel/tools/testing/selftests/cambyses/run.py

Requires Python 3 and a host C compiler (CC, default cc) with UBSan support.
The runner extracts actual fair.c code, compiles host-only harness binaries in
an automatically removed temporary directory, and runs the on/off x PREEMPT
on/off matrix. It does not build or boot a kernel.

CONFIG_SCHED_CAMBYSES_BUDGET is default n and a pure compile-time switch.
There is no runtime enable/off knob or live switching. With CONFIG=n the
original vendor detach_tasks function is retained; source and preprocessed
tokens are compared against baseline 97c1beea4278468ddea9f967019211c4330c6f03.

The enabled experiment implements strict task_h_load budgeting and a restricted
smallest-overshoot concession within the final scan slice only, and only before
any successful detach in that balance. This is NOT a per-balance global minimum.
LBF_NEED_BREAK is a pause: no concession is consumed, and references are released
before more_balance unlocks. Earlier slices' candidates are not cached.
Concession revalidation uses the actual migration eligibility predicate without
repeating scan accounting or affinity-retargeting side effects. Tests extract
both the migration predicate and detach_tasks from fair.c. Two negative controls
reintroduce the old pause-concession and double-hot-accounting defects and must
fail their corresponding C assertions.
It is NOT complete Cambyses. Full/block rotation is deferred; no successor is
cached across double_lock_balance. Tests cover budget, overshoot, vendor redo
reset, one-concession lifetime, candidate/target validation, and a simulated
lock-drop successor removal. Existing BORE/POC content outside the experiment
is checked against the baseline.

Host scaffolding does not reproduce real scheduler locking, WALT accounting,
or device behavior. Passing these tests does not establish device/WALT safety.
